tgs:Organization.CenterForPartnershipSystems a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Center for Partnership Systems"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "Center for Partnership Studies"@en ;
    skos:definition "Non-profit, led by Riane Eisler, that develops practical applications of her partnership research -- in education, economics (caring economics) and a partnership self-assessment toolkit -- and is associated with the Interdisciplinary Journal of Partnership Studies."@en ;
    dcterms:source <http://www.centerforpartnership.org/> ;
    dcterms:isReferencedBy tgs:Interview.TGS_116_RianeEisler ;
    .

tgs:Organization.PerspectiveDaily a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Perspective Daily"@en ;
    skos:definition "German ad-free online magazine for constructive journalism, founded in 2016 by Maren Urner and Han Langeslag; the first of its kind. Urner was editor-in-chief and managing director until March 2019."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://perspective-daily.de/> ;
    dcterms:isReferencedBy tgs:Interview.TGS_174_MarenUrner ;
    .

tgs:Organization.TompkinsConservation a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tompkins Conservation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Conservation organization founded by Kristine and Doug Tompkins that, with partners including its legacy groups Rewilding Chile and Rewilding Argentina, has protected about 15 million acres of parkland in Chile and Argentina, donating land to the two governments as national parks and reintroducing missing species such as the jaguar in Argentina's Iberá wetlands."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.tompkinsconservation.org/> ;
    dcterms:isReferencedBy tgs:Interview.TGS_170_KristineTompkins ;
    .

tgs:Organization.Patagonia a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Patagonia"@en ;
    skos:definition "Outdoor clothing company started by climber Yvon Chouinard in the early 1970s, which from the late 1970s treated the company as an asset for changing the world; Kristine Tompkins was its general manager and then CEO."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.patagonia.com/company-history/> ;
    dcterms:isReferencedBy tgs:Interview.TGS_170_KristineTompkins ;
    .

tgs:Organization.R30 a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "r3.0"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "Redesign for Resilience & Regeneration"@en ;
    skos:definition "Nonprofit platform for redesigning economic and social systems for resilience and regeneration, known for context-based sustainability metrics (measuring impact against thresholds and fair shares). Convened the Bioregional Carrying Capacity session series (2024-2026), where the Devon Doughnut and the California Doughnut were presented."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.r3-0.org/> ;
    .

tgs:Organization.CenterForNativePeoplesAndTheEnvironment a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Center for Native Peoples and the Environment"@en ;
    skos:definition "Center at SUNY College of Environmental Science and Forestry, founded by Robin Wall Kimmerer (now director emeritus), that brings Indigenous knowledge and Western science together in environmental education and research; Kimmerer cites it as one of the rare programs that teach Indigenous ethics within sustainability science."@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf tgs:AcademicInstitution.SUNYCollegeOfEnvironmentalScienceAndForestry ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.esf.edu/nativepeoples/> ;
    .

tgs:Organization.PlantBabyPlant a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Plant Baby Plant"@en ;
    skos:definition "Nonprofit founded by Robin Wall Kimmerer (founder and president of the board) and co-founders, named as an answer to 'drill, baby, drill': it encourages people to restore land with the tools of science, engineering and ecology, and to restore their relationship with land through the arts, as the motive force of what Kimmerer calls the Age of Remembering."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://plantbabyplant.com/about/> ;
    .

tgs:Organization.CitizenPotawatomiNation a thinkr:Organization, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Citizen Potawatomi Nation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Federally recognized tribal nation of the Potawatomi people, headquartered in Shawnee, Oklahoma, descended from Potawatomi removed from their Great Lakes homelands in the 1830s (including the 1838 Trail of Death). Robin Wall Kimmerer is an enrolled member."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.potawatomi.org/> ;
    .

